PURPOSE Evaluate the paper's separate vehicle and package pricing families and
    admit complete paths while preserving objective and solve-scope identities.
REFERENCES Paper Eqs. 32--40; GeneratingSubProblem.cs.
ASSUMPTIONS Vehicle pricing evaluates each existing reference-route context
    separately. These current-pool objectives do not define a fixed-row full-master
    pricing oracle; their status determines progress within the stated scope.
INPUT network, current optimal restricted-master dual bundle, pool, node,
    counter, config with pricing/support limits and tolerances.
OUTPUT PricingBatch{results,candidates,diagnostics,status,counter,signatures}.

PROCEDURE PriceSplitFamiliesLocal(network,duals,pool,node,counter,config)
    counter += 1.
    Require duals match this pool, row system, node and objective convention.
    results := empty; candidates := empty; diagnostics := empty.
    FOR every physical vehicle k
        contexts := current vehicle routes lRef with owner(lRef)=k.
        IF contexts is empty
            Record pricing_context_missing(k); CONTINUE.
        FOR every lRef in contexts
            If the global deadline is reached, record unrun_context and CONTINUE.
            context := (lRef,duals.rowSignature,pool.signature).
            result := SolveSeparateVehicleModel(network,k,duals,
                node.vehicleBranches,context,config.limits.pricing).
            Record result even if no incumbent exists.
            IF result has a valid candidate AND result.pricingObjective < -rcTolerance
                Add candidate tagged vehicle_pricing with its context records.
    FOR every active parent order r
        If the global deadline is reached, record unrun_package and CONTINUE.
        result := SolveSeparatePackageModel(network,r,duals,node.packageBranches,
            config.limits,config.includeSupportSeeds,node.vehicleBranches).
        Record pricing and support fields separately.
        IF result has a valid candidate AND result.pricingObjective < -rcTolerance
            Add its complete package route tagged package_pricing.
            Add audited supporting vehicle routes, if present, tagged support_seed.
    Determine whether every required vehicle context and every package model
        either terminated optimally with a valid audited incumbent and finite
        objective, or proved its declared operating/served-path model infeasible.
    Unused/unserved connectors are already present as permitted seed routes;
        they are not omitted unknown columns in these pricing calls.
    IF any context is missing, failed, incomplete or unaudited: status=pricing_open.
    ELSE IF any original pricing objective < -rcTolerance: status=negative_candidates.
    ELSE: status=split_pricing_stationary.
    RETURN PricingBatch{results,candidates,diagnostics,status,counter,signatures}.
    # stationary means the documented current-pool expressions are nonnegative.
    # This status carries no full-master LP bound or exact B&P certificate.
    Cap each solver call by the smaller of its configured limit and the remaining
        global budget. A skipped context makes status=pricing_open.

PROCEDURE PriceSplitFamilies(network,duals,pool,node,counter,config)
    RETURN PriceSplitFamiliesLocal(network,duals,pool,node,counter,config).
    # Alias for the same pricing procedure.

PROCEDURE InsertPricingResults(pool,batch,node,network,config)
    inserted := 0; duplicates := empty; rejected := empty.
    FOR every candidate in batch.candidates
        Require the recorded dual/pool/branch signatures match its generating solve.
        Validate the entire path, epoch commitments, cost and inherited branches.
        IF invalid: record rejection and reason; CONTINUE.
        identity := (kind,physical owner OR parent order,ordered original arc IDs,
                     linked package-fragment identities,catalog signature).
        IF identity exists in pool
            Record duplicate with its original pricing objective and context.
            IF its audited pricing objective is negative, mark negative_duplicate.
            CONTINUE.
        ExtractSplitColumns(candidate,initializationKind=candidate.tag).
        Insert d[q,r], g[l,k], d[l,r], arc incidences and original route cost;
            update every forward/transposed dictionary consistently.
        inserted += 1.
    Recompute pool signature if anything changed.
    RETURN AdmissionResult{pool,inserted,duplicates,rejected,
                          hasNegativeDuplicate,hasContractFailure}.

PROCEDURE ClassifyRound(batch,admission)
    IF admission.inserted > 0: RETURN progress; rebuild and resolve the master.
    IF admission.hasContractFailure: RETURN unresolved_candidate_validation.
    IF admission.hasNegativeDuplicate: RETURN unresolved_negative_duplicate.
    IF batch.status=split_pricing_stationary: RETURN stationary_current_pool.
    RETURN pricing_open with per-model termination reasons.

TERMINATION
    Equal route-cost sequences do not establish no progress: distinct paths can
        have equal cost. Progress uses admitted complete-route identities.
    Keep absent objectives unknown. Apply the reduced-cost threshold to the
        pricing objective. Preserve solver limits and unresolved contexts in the
        node record; terminate with their status when no progress is possible.
